# Wedding Announcement: each of Bot1's end steps it gets an invitation counter, then draws if Bot1 attacked with two or more
# creatures that turn (CR 508.1) and otherwise makes a 1/1 Human; at three counters it transforms (keeping them, CR 712.18)
# into Wedding Festivity, +1/+1 to Bot1's creatures only. T1: no attack, Human (1 counter). T3: two Ornithopters attack
# (exactly two), a card is drawn and no Human (2). T5: one attacks (its T3 attack does not count), Human, 3 counters, transform.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Wedding Announcement
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Plains
Plains x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Wedding Announcement.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Wedding Announcement.Counters.Invitation = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 7
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter#1 > Bot2; Ornithopter#2 > Bot2)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Wedding Announcement.Counters.Invitation = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 7
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 3
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter#1 > Bot2)
[T6 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Wedding Festivity.Counters.Invitation = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 8
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Human Token#1.Power = 2
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
